{"id": "EUVD-2026-103589", "enisaUuid": "ecbe0bf9-5f0a-3c79-be2c-2c5f243a79a0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbna: prevent IOC timer rearm during teardown\n\nbna: prevent IOC timer rearm during teardown\n\nbnad_pci_remove() and the probe disable_ioceth path call\ntimer_delete_sync() for ioc_timer, sem_timer and hb_timer, but not for\niocpf_timer.  bnad_iocpf_timeout() then takes bnad->bna_lock after\nfree_netdev() has freed the struct bnad.\n\nDeleting iocpf_timer last does not fix this.  sem_timer and\niocpf_timer rearm each other: bnad_iocpf_sem_timeout() can arm\niocpf_timer, and bnad_iocpf_timeout() arms sem_timer from\nbfa_ioc_hw_sem_get() when the semaphore is busy.\ntimer_delete_sync() only waits out its own callback.\nbnad_ioceth_disable() can time out and leave that callback live.\n\nShut all four IOC timers down with timer_shutdown_sync() on both\npaths, so a later mod_timer() is ignored.\n\nThis issue was identified during our ongoing static-analysis research\nwhile reviewing kernel code.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f04cbdfac9b8284146995ab7ba0d054ad1d20ec6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/28e32ace754b57534ef0ca0fb99bcbea5b13ba2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4d97a141e85a034566c33c7ed854c8a3e8a268f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e09d1c6729ee4a7812128902d9274ff565f958b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77b1718e39e5c9f6956fb60807326af20baf889d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-crgf-pp48-gvh7", "CVE-2026-98544"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "18ae8fb4-c7f9-3b72-945d-fa7c5621dc06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "43b7716b-f343-3453-9202-5ab230fc7b5f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "58023cb6-3100-3db4-84b1-e4a79b4eddd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d32f7696286eef9e5644eb57e79a36756274357 <e09d1c6729ee4a7812128902d9274ff565f958b8"}, {"id": "60dec973-e1c6-3163-bacf-3d5bbe9045c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d32f7696286eef9e5644eb57e79a36756274357 <28e32ace754b57534ef0ca0fb99bcbea5b13ba2a"}, {"id": "73e69885-a896-3583-abbe-49a9578710a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.38"}, {"id": "7592b00f-5a09-36da-9c9d-65bf1b9e915d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "81b40869-c2ef-38b4-ba34-2524d9c69dd0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "88f17f61-089a-3a72-bd4b-8f62b0394cbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d32f7696286eef9e5644eb57e79a36756274357 <f04cbdfac9b8284146995ab7ba0d054ad1d20ec6"}, {"id": "99e9fb28-9c4f-3224-b5ea-8a2a8e1dfe84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d32f7696286eef9e5644eb57e79a36756274357 <77b1718e39e5c9f6956fb60807326af20baf889d"}, {"id": "f126cd09-6ec9-3e6d-a2c7-7ca7e4344a92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ffaac979-1e36-363e-8781-46b761b63f57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1d32f7696286eef9e5644eb57e79a36756274357 <4d97a141e85a034566c33c7ed854c8a3e8a268f1"}, {"id": "ffb4d49f-8dd4-3205-8d1a-408e280f086a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6238d5f4-a195-3974-a73c-2cda4fb8b151", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}